sub:Head {
  this: a np:Nanopublication ;
    np:hasAssertion sub:assertion ;
    np:hasProvenance sub:provenance ;
    np:hasPublicationInfo sub:pubinfo .
}

sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/flight-allometry-law> a delphi:Concept, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "General allometry: measured exponents compose (W = a L^b) (Lean 4, kernel-checked)" ;
    dct:description "For power laws with real exponents the ratio between sizes is (L2/L1)^b, a quotient of power laws has exponent b1 − b2 (wing loading bW − bS), the cube law is the case b = 3, and under power laws for weight and area with constant air density and maximal lift coefficient the minimum flight speed has exponent (bW − bS)/2." ;
    dct:source "Proved in this project (lean/Delphi/Flight.lean) for the flying-fish audit and the physics thread's coupled simulator (hub items 3 and 4, 2026-10-31); hypotheses named, no paper states it in this form." ;
    skos:notation "f ∝ L^b ; W/S ∝ L^(bW−bS) ; v_min ∝ L^((bW−bS)/2)" ;
    skos:definition """/-- Under power laws for weight and lifting area with constant `ρ`, `C_L,max`, the minimum-speed exponent is `(b_W - b_S)/2`. With Davenport's exponents this is `(2.981 - 1.834)/2`, not the isometric `1/2`. -/
theorem vmin_powerLaw_log {W S : ℝ → ℝ} {aW bW aS bS ρ Cmax : ℝ} (hW : PowerLaw W aW bW) (hS : PowerLaw S aS bS)
    (hρ : 0 < ρ) (hCmax : 0 < Cmax) {L₁ L₂ : ℝ} (h₁ : 0 < L₁) (h₂ : 0 < L₂) :
    Real.log (vmin ρ Cmax (W L₂) (S L₂) / vmin ρ Cmax (W L₁) (S L₁)) = (bW - bS) / 2 * Real.log (L₂ / L₁)"""^^delphi:lean4 ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    delphi:leanDeclaration "Delphi.PowerLaw" ;
    delphi:leanTheorem "Delphi.vmin_powerLaw_log", "Delphi.powerLaw_ratio", "Delphi.powerLaw_log", "Delphi.powerLaw_div", "Delphi.cubeLaw_powerLaw" ;
    delphi:leanVerified "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    skos:scopeNote "The power-law form with a fixed exponent is itself the hypothesis; nothing here says a species obeys one." ;
    rdfs:comment "Status: kernel-checked (Lean 4 accepted the module with zero sorry and standard axioms only). Not expert-validated. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it; strict neutrality, constant population size, Wright-Fisher reproduction and independent mutant fates (Kimura), fixed fitnesses and haploid inheritance (Fisher), equal fecundity and a 1:1 sex ratio (Maynard Smith) are assumptions written in the module header, not conclusions. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the paper is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/Delphi/Flight.lean>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/flight-allometry-law> dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/flight-allometry-law> ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-flight-allometry-law> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-flight-allometry-law> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "Lean 4 kernel accepted Delphi.vmin_powerLaw_log with zero sorry and standard axioms, and rejected 1 deliberately broken variant(s)" ;
    dct:description "Build receipt. Lean (version 4.35.0, x86_64-w64-windows-gnu, commit eb6cafb7290e8bd5f2937522d8d804f58f02bafc, Release); toolchain leanprover/lean4:v4.35.0; Mathlib v4.35.0 (56a005855ea17e0b0958f73ec801ae140b0a1679). lake build exit 0 in 5.5 s with 0 errors; 0 sorry in lean/Delphi/Flight.lean (206 lines). #print axioms for Delphi.vmin_powerLaw_log, Delphi.powerLaw_ratio, Delphi.powerLaw_log, Delphi.powerLaw_div, Delphi.cubeLaw_powerLaw: Classical.choice, Quot.sound, propext only (Lean's standard axioms; no sorryAx). Mutation evidence (lean/mutate.mjs, 2026-10-31T21:00:09.361Z): 1 deliberate change(s) to the statement or the model were each rejected by the compiler: [allometry-quotient-sum] Mutant: a quotient of power laws claimed to have the SUM of the exponents instead of the difference. Rejected with 2 error(s): allometry-quotient-sum.lean:66:28: error: Tactic `rewrite` failed: Did not find an occurrence of the pattern Controls: 12 of 12 unmodified modules accepted by the same command." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/flight-allometry-law> ;
    rdfs:comment "This evidence item establishes that the stated theorem follows from the stated model. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it; strict neutrality, constant population size, Wright-Fisher reproduction and independent mutant fates (Kimura), fixed fitnesses and haploid inheritance (Fisher), equal fecundity and a 1:1 sex ratio (Maynard Smith) are assumptions written in the module header, not conclusions. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the paper is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/mutations.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/Delphi/Audit.lean> .
}

